content.text:
Because PR #568 removes packages that its own source still imports:

```ts
import ... from "@authfn/core";
import ... from "@authfn/lookup-cloudflare-do";
import ... from "@authfn/lookup-dynamodb";
```

After a clean install, those modules are absent, so account typechecking fails with `TS2307: Cannot find module ...`. :codex-annotation{index="1"}

Therefore the PR must do one of two things:

- Keep the old dependencies temporarily, leaving the current account implementation buildable.
- Include the account-source migration that replaces those imports with the new modular AuthFn APIs.

The issue is sequencing, not that the legacy dependencies should remain permanently. Every stacked PR must compile independently; otherwise PR #568 is broken until a later PR happens to repair it.

